aeat_rege
=========

The aeat_rege module of the Tryton application platform.

Regime levels are named Basic and Advanced. The stored key for Basic remains
``normal`` for compatibility with existing periods and integrations.

Advanced REGE invoicing
-----------------------

Configure a dedicated revenue journal on each group with advanced periods.
For every participating company and fiscal year, configure customer invoice
and customer credit note sequences in Journal Sequences. Do not reuse the
ordinary invoice sequences. Missing configuration blocks validation/numbering.
Existing groups need their journal configured after upgrading the module.

Membership and regime periods are evaluated using the invoice date, falling
back to the accounting date and then today. Membership ending dates are
inclusive fiscal dates: for an exclusion effective during May, set April 30
as the last REGE date. Eligibility, elections and their statutory deadlines
must be checked before entering the fiscal dates.

Enter the attributable VAT-bearing unit cost explicitly on each advanced
intragroup invoice line, including supplier invoices. A missing cost blocks
saving even in draft; a justified explicit zero is allowed. Product inventory cost and the
commercial price are not automatic substitutes for fiscal cost. Allocate
investment goods within their statutory regularization periods before entering
the cost. Keep supporting allocation calculations with the invoice documents.

The cost determines VAT and tax bases in accounting. The commercial price
continues to determine revenue/payables. Supplier deductibility affects only
deductible VAT, not the cost base. Enter zero explicitly for operations with no
attributable fiscal cost. Imported/generated lines must also supply their
fiscal costs; taxes do not supply a cost or an exclusion default.

Advanced REGE invoices omit automatic accounting tax rows whose base and amount
are both zero. Exempt or zero-rate rows with a nonzero base and manual rows are
preserved. The read-only fiscal summary shows the commercial base, fiscal cost,
VAT by tax and, for purchases, deductible and non-deductible VAT. Non-deductible
VAT is already included in the expense and must not be added to the total again.
SII reconstructs zero-cost fiscal details from invoice lines, independently of
the persisted accounting tax rows. Existing draft rows disappear when taxes are
recomputed; posted invoices and stored SII submissions are not rewritten.

When account_reports is installed, this module extends Taxes by Invoice in
HTML/PDF and Excel with commercial and cost bases, including zero-cost services.
The optional report integration, labels and tests belong entirely to aeat_rege;
account_reports retains its standard behavior when aeat_rege is not installed.

General VAT Unit Value optionally records a valuation under articles 78 and 79
different from the commercial price; it does not change the amount payable.
REGE Exemption Waived records the election for the individual operation and
requires selection of the applicable VAT tax. It does not choose a tax rate.
The standard account_invoice ODT report and the standard html_report invoice
display both bases, the REGE notice and the applicable notices per operation.
Exemption notices come from the configured taxes and coexist with REGE; they
are not inferred from a zero cost or zero VAT amount. Waiver notices apply
only to the explicitly marked lines. Configure the exemption legal notice on
the tax, including the relevant article. With SII, E1 provides an article 20
fallback when the tax has no more specific notice.

The cediv and imi layouts reuse the HTML summary supplied by aeat_rege. Custom ODT
templates and HTML layouts overriding the standard footer must integrate
invoice.get_rege_report_data() or REGEReportMixin.show_rege_summary(record).
The data API returns bases (label/amount pairs), legal_notice and line_notices
(description/notice pairs). This lets custom layouts preserve their design.
No change to the invoice comment or persisted tax amounts is made by printing.

SII uses the invoice's computed taxes and reports the cost base independently
of the recipient's deduction percentage. The advanced regime uses key 06.
In accordance with the AEAT SII common registration FAQ, BaseImponible contains
the general valuation under articles 78 and 79, BaseImponibleACoste contains
the REGE cost and the VAT amount is calculated on that cost.
Reference: https://sede.agenciatributaria.gob.es/Sede/impuestos-tasas/iva/iva-libros-registro-iva-traves-aeat/preguntas-frecuentes/2-registro-cuestiones-comunes.html

Upgrade notes
-------------

The former cost-base exclusion flag is removed from invoice lines, taxes and
tax templates. During upgrade, all previously excluded lines receive an
explicit cost of zero, including lines with a nonzero stored cost: the flag
previously overrode that cost. Non-excluded lines keep their original costs.
The obsolete columns and views are removed. This migration is idempotent and
does not recalculate invoice amounts, accounting moves or submitted SII data.
Review integrations that supplied the removed flag and send explicit costs.

The legacy REGE exemption purchase/sale taxes expire on 2026-09-30 (inclusive).
On module upgrade, taxes linked to the former REGE templates are marked as
legacy, detached from their templates and given that end date. An earlier
existing end date is preserved. The removed XML templates and their tax-code
line templates are deleted by Tryton's module update. Existing business taxes,
tax-code lines and invoice/move references remain available for historical use.
This migration is idempotent and applies across companies.

Validation and numbering reject legacy taxes after their end date, including
taxes assigned by products/rules or manual invoice tax rows. Update those
defaults to the VAT tax applicable to the operation. No new legacy taxes are
created by chart installation. Copies without a link to the original templates
must be reviewed separately; taxes are not identified by their translated name.

For the headphones example, enter commercial prices 85.96 and 8.60, REGE costs
85.96 and 0.00, the ordinary 21% purchase VAT on both lines and a deductible
rate of 0 for the recipient. The result is 112.61 payable, 18.05 VAT incurred
and zero deductible VAT. SII reports key 06, general base 94.56, cost base
85.96 and VAT rate 21%; it does not report an E6 exemption or a zero-rate line.
The upgrade does not amend posted invoices or resend SII records.

Update aeat_rege and cediv, configure the group journals and fiscal-year
sequences, then review draft invoices before posting. Costs previously filled
with zero by cediv cannot be distinguished automatically from justified zeros;
review them against their source documents. Previously posted invoices and
SII submissions require reconciliation before any correction or resubmission.

This module does not generate forms 039, 322 or 353, an analytical memorandum,
investment allocation schedules or differentiated-sector pro-rata returns.

